{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_40","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"fetch","tool":"fetch","arguments":{"max_length":5000,"raw":false,"start_index":0,"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022%E2%80%932023_Brazilian_election_protests"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Contents of https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022%E2%80%932023_Brazilian_election_protests:\n| 2022–2023 Brazilian election protests | |\n| --- | --- |\n| Part of the [2022 Brazilian coup plot](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Brazilian_coup_plot \"2022 Brazilian coup plot\") | |\n| Truckers protesting against the result of the 2022 presidential elections in the BR-381, [Timóteo](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timóteo_(municipality) \"Timóteo (municipality)\"), Minas Gerais | |\n| Date | 30 October 2022 – [8 January 2023](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8_January_Brasília_attacks \"8 January Brasília attacks\") (2 months, 1 week and 2 days) |\n| Location | Brazil   * 25 states and the [Federal District](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_District_(Brazil) \"Federal District (Brazil)\") |\n| Caused by | * Victory of [Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Luiz_Inácio_Lula_da_Silva \"Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva\") in the [2022 Brazilian general election](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Brazilian_general_election \"2022 Brazilian general election\") * False claims of electoral fraud made by then-president [Jair Bolsonaro](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jair_Bolsonaro \"Jair Bolsonaro\") and his allies * Distrust in the electoral process, congress and judiciary * Right-wing extremism in Brazil |\n| Goals | * Contest or overturn President-elect Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva's victory in the election * Interfere with the transition of the presidency to Lula da Silva * Maintenance, or return, of Jair Bolsonaro as [President of Brazil](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/President_of_Brazil \"President of Brazil\") * Military intervention against president-elect Lula da Silva |\n| Methods | * Protest: [picketing](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Picketing \"Picketing\"), [political demonstrations](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political_demonstration \"Political demonstration\"), [Internet activism](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_activism \"Internet activism\"), [barricades](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Barricade \"Barricade\"), [roadblocks](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roadblock \"Roadblock\") and [street blockades](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blockade \"Blockade\") * [direct action](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Direct_action \"Direct action\"): strikes, [civil disobedience](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_disobedience \"Civil disobedience\") and [civil resistance](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_resistance \"Civil resistance\") * [Civil disorder](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Civil_disorder \"Civil disorder\"): [Political violence](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Political_violence \"Political violence\"), riots, vandalism, arson, [occupation](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occupation_(protest) \"Occupation (protest)\") of public buildings and [looting](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Looting \"Looting\") * [Terrorism](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Right-wing_terrorism \"Right-wing terrorism\"): [bomb threats](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bomb_threat \"Bomb threat\") and [attempted bombing](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Improvised_explosive_device \"Improvised explosive device\") |\n| Result | Protests concluded  * Attempts to overturn the [2022 presidential election](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2022_Brazilian_general_election \"2022 Brazilian general election\") failed * Protesters fail to organize large-scale dissent or affect the transition of power * Congress, [Supreme Court](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supreme_Federal_Court \"Supreme Federal Court\") and [Electoral Court](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superior_Electoral_Court \"Superior Electoral Court\") certify Lula's victory in the 2022 election * Protests, blockades and camps eventually subsided or dismantled * Increased security in government buildings during and after the 2023 presidential inauguration * [Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva becomes President of Brazil](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Third_inauguration_of_Luiz_Inácio_Lula_da_Silva \"Third inauguration of Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva\") for his third mandate * [Rioters storm the Praça dos Três Poderes](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8_January_Brasília_attacks \"8 January Brasília attacks\") in Brasília * Mass arrests and dismantlement of blockades and camps in response to violent attacks by protesters * [Jair Bolsonaro](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jair_Bolsonaro \"Jair Bolsonaro\") acknowledges defeat in the 2022 presidential election and formally condemns the [8 January attacks](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8_January_Brasília_attacks \"8 January Brasília attacks\") * Instauration of the [8 January CPMI](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/8_January_CPMI \"8 January CPMI\") and federal investigations against ex-president Jair Bolsonaro and close allies * Small-scale protests continue into the [Lula presidency](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Second_presidency_of_Lula_da_Silva \"Second presidency of Lula da Silva\") |\n| Parties | |\n| |  |  | | --- | --- | | Pro-Bolsonaro groups and sympathizers   * Pro-gun activists[[1]](#cite_note-1) | [Law enforcement](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law_enforcement_in_Brazil \"Law enforcement in Brazil\")   * [Federal Highway Police](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Highway_Police_(Brazil) \"Federal Highway Police (Brazil)\")   + Riot Police Component[[2]](#cite_note-2) * [Military Police](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mi\n\n<error>Content truncated. Call the fetch tool with a start_index of 5000 to get more content.</error>"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
